ader of `scanner_goldens.cljc` and `scan_test.cljc` for how; keep the owner's rule: goldens are regenerated by a mechanical, recomputable procedure, never hand-edited) and put the diff and its explanation in the report; if it is a scanner bug, fix the scanner and say so. Do not regenerate other groups.\nAlso run `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` (JVM) and report: master carries 08a3a722 which fixed that suite's readers for the admission default; shiva's Dart slow lane failed two of its tests on `srvm-phase7` BEFORE this merge: tell me if they pass here on the JVM.\nVerification, ALL foreground, JVM only: `clj -M:kondo --lint` on changed files; `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n dao.jing.hash-registry-contract-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.scan-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-custody-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.layout-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test`; then every `yin.vm.ucf.*` namespace and the whole `dao.jing.*` family (report counts; the only acceptable remaining red is `cbor-conformance-test/no-source-file-that-names-the-resource-writes-files` IF it still fails on master, check). Mutants (cp backup; diff and `git diff --quiet` to verify): revert each fixed site to the equality form (the lint must fail); a carrier row id with a non-BLAKE3 prefix accepted; a SHA-256 install address refused. Do not commit. Report `collab/1792570000000-engineer-p7m-lint-scan.report.md`: per site the change and why, the scan diff and explanation, counts, mutants, anything uncertain.\n","numLines":8,"startLine":1,"totalLines":8}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XwUN38khunzSq3c818UHxY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
